		new("earlymodern_religious_hindu_sacred_thread", "thread", "a fine $colour cotton shoulder thread", "Several fine strands of $colour cotton form this long, closed loop of thread. They lie alongside one another with a slight twist, gathering into a compact knot where their ends are joined. The loop is long enough to pass over one shoulder and fall diagonally across the torso. Its unadorned strands have a soft, slightly fibrous surface, without beads, a clasp or a separate pendant.", SizeCategory.VerySmall, ItemQuality.Good, 15, 24.0m, true, "cotton", ["Era / Early Modern Era", "Market / Clothing / Standard Clothing", "Market / Religious Goods / Ritual Supplies"], ["Holdable", "Destroyable_Clothing", "Wear_Bandolier", "Armour_LightClothing", "Insulation_Minor", "Variable_Colour"], "Canonical Renaissance stock item with an authored full description."),
