		new("earlymodern_religious_zoroastrian_prayer_cap", "cap", "a plain $colour cotton prayer cap", "This close-fitting cap is sewn from light $colour cotton into a low, rounded crown. Narrow seams run upward from a neatly bound lower edge, shaping the cloth without a projecting brim. A thin lining follows the same outline inside, covering the raw edges of the joins. The outer surface is plain and softly flexible, with no badge, tassel or embroidered band around the brow.", SizeCategory.Small, ItemQuality.Good, 70, 40.0m, true, "cotton", ["Era / Early Modern Era", "Market / Clothing / Standard Clothing", "Market / Religious Goods / Ritual Supplies"], ["Holdable", "Destroyable_Clothing", "Wear_Skullcap", "Armour_LightClothing", "Insulation_Minor", "Variable_Colour"], "Canonical Renaissance stock item with an authored full description."),
